usage: textkit convert [--from label] [--to label] [--strict] [--dump raw|hex|base64] [--labels] [--buffer n] [--limit bytes] [file...]
Options:
  --from <str>    The input's encoding, by any label of the Encoding Standard (default utf-8)
  --to <str>      The output's encoding, by any label of the Encoding Standard (default utf-8)
  --strict        Stop at the first malformed byte instead of writing U+FFFD; reads each input whole
  --dump <str>    Write the output bytes as raw, hex or base64 (default raw)
  --labels        Print the encoding each line of the input names, instead of converting
  --buffer <int>  The read buffer, in bytes (default 16384)
  --limit <int>   With --strict, the most bytes to read, all inputs together (default 8388608)
Arguments:
  <files>...      Files to read; none, or -, is standard input
